WARDEN_USAGE=$(cat <<'USAGE'
\033[33mUsage:\033[0m
  d1-pull [label]           Copies the LIVE Cloudflare D1 database into the LOCAL one

  Steps: backs up the local database (backups/...-before-pull.sql), exports the live one to
  backups/d1-ledger-remote-<timestamp>-<label>.sql, replaces the local database with it, restarts the app.
  The live database is only read. Needs CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN and CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID in .env.
  Document files in R2 are not copied (only their records). Live accounts and sessions come along,
  so you can sign in locally with your live password.

\033[33mOptions:\033[0m
  -h, --help        Display this help menu
USAGE
)
